      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: -942.84235, y: 399.26843}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 15134834976047125082
          m_Value1: 7451722965250884038
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'This HP threshold node has an "Abort Target"

          of none. This
          means that nothing will happen

          at the moment the enemy drops
          to 50%, but

          rather the next time the enemy selects a move,

          this
          option will become available.'
    - rid: 7865913011368886632
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: -641.44745, y: 396.67383}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 4148627016891837540
          m_Value1: 2578599644773322670
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'TODO CYRENE: Finish Code Implementation.


          Conversely, the
          Abort Target of "Both" will

          cause the graph to immediately begin
          trying to

          active this ability. It is important to note that

          the
          graph will parse from left to right, so

          especially with abilities
          that can overtake others

          it is imperative to ensure that the
          highest priority

          abilities are on the left side of the Try In
          Order

          node.'
